N0005,2016-02-01,health,WHO declares Zika virus a global public health emergency,The World Health Organization declared the spread of Zika virus and its suspected link to birth defects a Public Health Emergency of International Concern. The virus was spreading rapidly across the Americas.,TRUE,Real event (summarised from public reporting)
N0006,2016-02-07,agriculture,Government raises minimum support price for rabi crops; farmers in Karnataka cautious,"DELHI, Feb 7 — The Union cabinet approved an increase in the minimum support price for key rabi crops, with wheat rising by Rs 126 per quintal. Farmer groups in Karnataka said the hike was welcome but did not fully offset higher fertiliser and fuel costs. “The data over the next two quarters will be crucial,” said Anita Collins, a police spokesperson.",TRUE,Synthetic (fictional outlet): The Metro Ledger
N0007,2016-02-11,local,Lucknow metro extension of 21 km opens to commuters,"LUCKNOW, Feb 11 — A 21-km stretch of the Lucknow metro was opened to the public on Thursday, with trains running every 7 minutes in peak hours. Officials expect daily ridership to rise by about 83,000 passengers.",TRUE,Synthetic (fictional outlet): The Civic Post
N0008,2016-02-11,environment,"Guwahati receives 182 mm rain in 24 hours; schools shut, traffic hit","GUWAHATI, Feb 11 — Heavy rain lashed Guwahati on Thursday, with the weather department recording 182 mm in 24 hours. Waterlogging was reported in several low-lying areas, suburban services ran late and authorities asked residents to avoid unnecessary travel. An orange alert remains in place for the next 48 hours.",TRUE,Synthetic (fictional outlet): The Weekly Record
N0009,2016-02-11,health,Chennai reports 100 dengue cases this month; health officials step up fogging,"CHENNAI, Feb 11 — The health department said Chennai has recorded 100 confirmed dengue cases so far this month, up from 60 in the same month last year. Fogging drives and door-to-door surveys have been intensified, and residents have been urged to clear stagnant water. “Our priority is to ensure that people are not inconvenienced,” said Imran Joshi, a police spokesperson.",TRUE,Synthetic (fictional outlet): Deccan Dispatch
N0010,2016-02-13,world,Inflation in Sydney eases to 5.3% as fuel prices cool,"SYDNEY, Feb 13 — Authorities in Sydney announced the decision on Saturday after months of consultation with businesses and residents. Supporters called it overdue, while some retailers said they needed more time to adapt. “We will monitor the situation closely and update residents as needed,” said Latha Bennett, a professor of public policy.",TRUE,Synthetic (fictional outlet): Daily Horizon
N0011,2016-02-14,education,Kochi university introduces 3 new job-oriented degree courses from next session,"KOCHI, Feb 14 — A state university in Kochi has approved 3 new undergraduate and postgraduate programmes in areas such as data science, renewable energy and healthcare management, beginning from the next academic session. Admissions will be through an entrance test. “We will monitor the situation closely and update residents as needed,” said Suresh Okafor, the association's general secretary.",TRUE,Synthetic (fictional outlet): The Metro Ledger
N0017,2016-03-08,politics,Mumbai civic body clears Rs 858 crore budget for roads and drainage,"MUMBAI, Mar 8 — The municipal corporation in Mumbai on Tuesday approved a budget outlay of Rs 858 crore for road repairs and storm-water drainage. Officials said work on 12 priority stretches will begin once tenders are finalised. “Our priority is to ensure that people are not inconvenienced,” said Laura Patel, a police spokesperson.",TRUE,Synthetic (fictional outlet): The Metro Ledger
N0020,2016-03-18,economy,Meridian Foods net profit rises 24% in second quarter,"MUMBAI, Mar 18 — Meridian Foods reported a 24% increase in net profit for the second quarter compared with the same period last year, citing softer demand in urban markets. Shares of the company gained about 5% in early trade. “We will monitor the situation closely and update residents as needed,” said Vikram Banerjee, a senior district official.",TRUE,Synthetic (fictional outlet): The Capital Courier
