N0028,2016-04-26,health,Indore reports 180 dengue cases this month; health officials step up fogging,"INDORE, Apr 26 — The health department said Indore has recorded 180 confirmed dengue cases so far this month, up from 108 in the same month last year. Fogging drives and door-to-door surveys have been intensified, and residents have been urged to clear stagnant water. “The numbers are encouraging, though it is too early to call it a trend,” said Grace Sharma, a senior district official.",TRUE,Synthetic (fictional outlet): Sunrise Bulletin
