N0001,2016-01-09,entertainment,Famous film star dead in accident? Family hiding the truth,"A page claims a well-known public figure has met with a serious accident or illness and that the family is hiding the news. The page names no hospital, gives no source and asks readers to 'like and share to pay respects'. The claim has been circulating as a hoax for years.",FAKE,"Synthetic (blog post, fictional): WakeUpNow Network"
N0002,2016-01-18,science,"BREAKING: Kochi will be underwater by next month, scientists warn","A widely shared message claims 'top scientists' have predicted a catastrophe within weeks and that governments are covering it up. No scientist or institution is named. Official forecasts show nothing of the sort, and the 'confirmation' cannot be found on any agency website.",FAKE,"Synthetic (forwarded message, fictional): FreedomLeaks Forum"
N0003,2016-01-22,economy,"New law: Rs 7,000 fine for using WhatsApp after 10 pm","A message doing the rounds says that from Monday banks will be shut and ATMs will run out of cash, so everyone should withdraw their savings immediately. The message cites no circular, gazette notification or regulator, and officials have denied it.",FAKE,"Synthetic (website, fictional): ShareThisFast"
N0004,2016-02-01,economy,"New law: Rs 2,000 fine for using WhatsApp after 10 pm","A message doing the rounds says that from Monday banks will be shut and ATMs will run out of cash, so everyone should withdraw their savings immediately. The message cites no circular, gazette notification or regulator, and officials have denied it.",FAKE,"Synthetic (messaging group forward, fictional): BreakingAlert Today"
N0012,2016-02-16,science,"Earth to go dark for 5 days next month, space agency confirms","A widely shared message claims 'top scientists' have predicted a catastrophe within weeks and that governments are covering it up. No scientist or institution is named. Official forecasts show nothing of the sort, and the 'confirmation' cannot be found on any agency website.",FAKE,"Synthetic (messaging group forward, fictional): TruthBlast24"
N0013,2016-02-28,health,"Plastic rice and fake eggs flooding Bengaluru markets, video shows",A video shared thousands of times shows a person holding a ball of 'plastic rice' and claims such products are being sold in Bengaluru. Food safety officials who tested samples found nothing unusual; the clip appears to be from an unrelated cooking demonstration.,FAKE,"Synthetic (forwarded message, fictional): HiddenFacts Daily"
N0014,2016-03-02,education,"Exams cancelled across Maharashtra for entire year, leaked circular reveals","A 'leaked circular' claims that all board exams in Maharashtra have been cancelled and students will be promoted automatically. The document has spelling mistakes, no reference number and no official signature; the board has called it fake.",FAKE,"Synthetic (blog post, fictional): The Secret Report"
N0015,2016-03-03,sports,"Mumbai club star banned for life for match fixing, sources say","Unnamed 'sources' claim the club's captain has been banned for life after a secret match-fixing probe. The club and the league have issued no statement, and the post cites no document, official or evidence.",FAKE,"Synthetic (blog post, fictional): BreakingAlert Today"
N0016,2016-03-07,health,"Scientists in Lagos 'confirm' turmeric milk reverses migraine, say sources","According to sources close to a research team, a study has quietly confirmed that turmeric milk can reverse migraine. The researchers, who asked not to be named, said the findings were being kept from the public. No journal, institution or data was provided.",FAKE,"Synthetic (forwarded message, fictional): WakeUpNow Network"
N0018,2016-03-11,sports,"Ahmedabad club star banned for life for match fixing, sources say","Unnamed 'sources' claim the club's captain has been banned for life after a secret match-fixing probe. The club and the league have issued no statement, and the post cites no document, official or evidence.",FAKE,"Synthetic (website, fictional): WakeUpNow Network"
N0019,2016-03-17,health,"New mobile towers in Kolkata are making people sick, residents claim","A video circulating in Kolkata claims that newly installed mobile towers are causing headaches and illness among nearby residents. The speaker, who does not give his name, says 'the authorities are hiding the radiation reports'. No medical or technical evidence is shown.",FAKE,"Synthetic (video channel, fictional): ShareThisFast"
N0022,2016-03-29,health,"SHOCKING: Drink raw papaya every morning and arthritis gone in 9 days, doctors hate this!","A 'retired doctor' reveals the trick pharma companies don't want you to know: raw papaya cures arthritis completely in just 9 days. No tests, no medicines. Thousands have already been cured but hospitals are hiding the truth. SHARE with everyone you love before this gets deleted!!!",FAKE,"Synthetic (blog post, fictional): BreakingAlert Today"
N0025,2016-04-12,technology,Free 5G upgrade: tap this link to get 10x speed on any phone,"A viral post promotes an app or link that promises impossible features. The link leads to a page asking for phone number, OTP and card details. Cyber-security experts say it is a phishing scam designed to steal money and data.",FAKE,"Synthetic (video channel, fictional): BreakingAlert Today"
